1858,http://neurovault.org/collections/1858/,http://neurovault.org/collections/1858/download,1294,,mperino2,4,Letting the good times roll: adolescence as a period of reduced inhibition to appetitive social cues,,10.1093/scan/nsw096,,"Michael T. Perino, Michelle E. Miernicki and Eva H. Telzer",http://scan.oxfordjournals.org/lookup/doi/10.1093/scan/nsw096,Social Cognitive and Affective Neuroscience,"This study examined the neural regions that were correlated with behavioral disinhibition in a normative adolescent sample, as well as functional connectivity during said disinhibition. It was conducted under the direction of Dr. Eva Telzer and can be found in the following publication (Perino, M. T., Miernicki, M. E., & Telzer, E. H. (2016). Letting the good times roll: adolescence as a period of reduced inhibition to appetitive social cues. Social cognitive and affective neuroscience, nsw096.",,False,2016-09-19T20:56:45.924246+02:00,2018-06-30T07:38:15.502939+02:00,2016-09-19T20:56:45.923753+02:00,,,,,,,,,,,,both,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,True,,True,False,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,[]
