3501,http://neurovault.org/collections/3501/,http://neurovault.org/collections/3501/download,2277,,matthew.kempton,6,"Meta-analysis of regional white matter volume in bipolar disorder with replication in an independent sample using coordinates, T-maps, and individual MRI data",,10.1016/j.neubiorev.2017.11.005,,"Stefania Pezzoli, Louise Emsell, Sarah W. Yip, Danai Dima, Panteleimon Giannakopoulos, Mojtaba Zarei, Stefania Tognin, Danilo Arnone, Anthony James, Sven Haller, Sophia Frangou, Guy M. Goodwin, Colm McDonald and Matthew J. Kempton",http://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S0149763417304906,Neuroscience & Biobehavioral Reviews,"Converging evidence suggests that bipolar disorder (BD) is associated with white matter (WM) abnormalities.
