5065,http://neurovault.org/collections/5065/,http://neurovault.org/collections/5065/download,6015,,thoern,38,The cerebellum is involved in processing of predictions and prediction errors in a fear conditioning paradigm,,10.7554/eLife.46831,,"Thomas Michael Ernst, Anna Evelina Brol, Marcel Gratz, Christoph Ritter, Ulrike Bingel, Marc Schlamann, Stefan Maderwald, Harald H Quick, Christian Josef Merz and Dagmar Timmann",https://elifesciences.org/articles/46831,eLife,"Prediction errors are thought to drive associative fear learning. Surprisingly little is known about the possible contribution of the cerebellum. To address this question, healthy participants underwent a differential fear conditioning paradigm during 7T magnetic resonance imaging. 

