1057,http://neurovault.org/collections/1057/,http://neurovault.org/collections/1057/download,15,,yeoyeo02,5,The organization of the human cerebral cortex estimated by intrinsic functional connectivity,,10.1152/jn.00338.2011,,"B. T. Thomas Yeo, Fenna M. Krienen, Jorge Sepulcre, Mert R. Sabuncu, Danial Lashkari, Marisa Hollinshead, Joshua L. Roffman, Jordan W. Smoller, Lilla Zöllei, Jonathan R. Polimeni, Bruce Fischl, Hesheng Liu and Randy L. Buckner",http://www.physiology.org/doi/10.1152/jn.00338.2011,Journal of Neurophysiology,"Resting state fMRI data from 1000 subjects were registered using surface-based alignment. A clustering approach was employed to identify and replicate 7 and 17 networks of functionally coupled regions across the cerebral cortex. The results revealed local networks confined to sensory and motor cortices as well as distributed networks of association regions that form interdigitated circuits. Within the sensory and motor cortices, functional connectivity followed topographic representations across adjacent areas. In association cortex, the connectivity patterns often showed abrupt transitions between network boundaries, forming largely parallel circuits.",https://github.com/ThomasYeoLab/CBIG/tree/master/stable_projects/brain_parcellation/Yeo2011_fcMRI_clustering,False,2016-01-03T05:15:58.273250+01:00,2018-06-30T11:07:59.137038+02:00,2016-01-03T05:25:27.306286+01:00,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,[]
1015,http://neurovault.org/collections/1015/,http://neurovault.org/collections/1015/download,833,,KirstieJane,294,Functional MRI of emotional memory in adolescent depression,,10.1016/j.dcn.2015.12.013,,"Rosemary J. Holt, Julia M. Graham, Kirstie J. Whitaker, Cindy C. Hagan, Cinly Ooi, Paul O. Wilkinson, Adrienne O. van Nieuwenhuizen, Belinda R. Lennox, Barbara J. Sahakian, Ian M. Goodyer, Edward T. Bullmore and John Suckling",http://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S1878929315001322,Developmental Cognitive Neuroscience,"Introduction: Major Depressive Disorder (MDD) is a leading cause of disease burden worldwide. Mood-congruent biases in memory tasks are frequently reported in MDD patients, with facilitated memory for negative stimuli. Most functional MRI studies to date have examined the neural correlates of these biases in depressed adults, with fewer studies in adolescents with MDD. Investigation of MDD in adolescence may aid greater understanding of the aetiology and development of the disorder. 
Methods: Cognitive biases were investigated in 56 MDD patients aged 11-17 years and a matched group of 30 healthy control participants with a self-referential memory task. Behavioural performance and BOLD fMRI data were collected during both encoding and retrieval stages. 
Results: The neural response to encoding in adolescents with MDD was found to differ significantly from controls. Additionally, neural responses during encoding and retrieval showed differential relationships with age between patient and control groups, specifically in medial, temporal, and prefrontal regions. 
Conclusions: These findings suggest that during adolescence neurophysiological activity associated with emotional memory differs in those with depression compared to controls and may be age sensitive. ",,False,2015-12-14T17:43:37.054857+01:00,2018-06-30T06:41:55.332801+02:00,2016-01-26T23:05:33.712046+01:00,eventrelated,1.0,120.0,12.9,,variable,False,,15.73,11.82,17.96,both,0.228,See Holt et al 2016,,True,See Holt et al 2016,Siemens,Trio TIM,3.0,EPI,None,192.0,64.0,3.75,0.75,AC-PC,interleaved,2000.0,30.0,78.0,FEAT,6.0,motion correction; slice-timing correction; non-brain removal; spatial smoothing; grand-mean intensity normalisation; highpass temporal filtering,Visual inspection,False,,True,,True,MCFLIRT,middle,,,False,True,FSL,nonlinear,FNIRT,,trilinear,T1,True,FLIRT,mni,MNI152_T1_2mm.nii.gz,2.0,True,gaussian,6.0,2.0,regression,general least squares,,gamma,True,False,True,False,False,,True,"Gaussian-weighted least-squares straight line fitting, with sigma=45.0s",none,regression,generalized least squares,,randommixedeffects,,False,,,,,,,[]
