190,http://neurovault.org/collections/190/,http://neurovault.org/collections/190/download,140,,alexschaefer83,1,Serotonergic Modulation of Intrinsic Functional Connectivity,,10.1016/j.cub.2014.08.024,,"Alexander Schaefer, Inga Burmann, Ralf Regenthal, Katrin Arélin, Claudia Barth, André Pampel, Arno Villringer, Daniel S. Margulies and Julia Sacher",http://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S0960982214010379,Current Biology,"Serotonin functions as an essential neuromodulator that serves a multitude of roles, most prominently balancing mood [ 1 ]. Serotonergic challenge has been observed to reduce intrinsic functional connectivity in brain regions implicated in mood regulation [ 2–4 ]. However, the full scope of serotonergic action on functional connectivity in the human brain has not been explored. Here, we show evidence that a single dose of a serotonin reuptake inhibitor dramatically alters functional connectivity throughout the whole brain in healthy subjects (n = 22). Our network-centrality analysis reveals a widespread decrease in connectivity in most cortical and subcortical areas. In the cerebellum and thalamus, however, we find localized increases. These rapid and brain-encompassing connectivity changes linked to acute serotonin transporter blockade suggest a key role for the serotonin transporter in the modulation of the functional macroscale connectome.",,False,2014-10-29T07:39:16.336198+01:00,2018-06-30T06:09:21.470577+02:00,2014-10-29T07:39:16.336198+01:00,other,,,,,,,,,,,,,,2.0,True,,Siemens,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,True,,linear,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,[]
