11982,http://neurovault.org/collections/11982/,http://neurovault.org/collections/11982/download,10137,,tanhuixin,12,Does Losing Money Really Hurt? Shared Neural Circuits Between Monetary Loss and Pain,,,,,,,"Both monetary loss and pain have been studied for decades, but evidence to support the relationship between them is still lacking. Here, we conducted a meta-analysis to explore the overlapping brain regions between monetary loss and pain, including physical pain and social pain. Results showed that irrespective of the type of pain experienced, activation of the anterior insula was a shared neural representation of monetary loss and pain. ",,False,2021-12-10T15:04:41.899476+01:00,2022-01-25T04:48:08.061539+01:00,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,[]
